WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.799
Any Vaccine cards?

00:08.466 --> 00:09.384
No.

00:10.468 --> 00:11.886
What are we gonna do?

00:21.229 --> 00:22.105
What's wrong?

00:23.106 --> 00:24.107
You look pale.

00:26.026 --> 00:27.193
I'm fine.

00:27.277 --> 00:28.945
Be honest.

00:30.447 --> 00:33.450
Are you a zombie?

00:36.953 --> 00:39.205
Yes, I am.

00:39.289 --> 00:40.582
He was hiding it!

00:40.665 --> 00:42.417
No! I was going to tell you.

00:42.500 --> 00:44.919
And I remember the guy who turned me.

00:47.213 --> 00:48.673
Let's shoot that zombie.

00:50.759 --> 00:51.843
You're up next.

00:53.928 --> 00:56.264
- Go kill that zombie.
- What?

00:58.349 --> 00:59.934
Have someone else do it.

01:00.769 --> 01:02.562
He's basically just a kid.

01:03.646 --> 01:05.398
No, you don't have to go.

01:05.982 --> 01:09.903
That's not fair to those
who dutifully used their Shotgun cards.

01:12.572 --> 01:15.867
You think anyone here
wants to kill people?

01:17.619 --> 01:19.496
We shouldn't kill each other.

01:24.375 --> 01:25.710
Then what about you?

01:26.419 --> 01:29.297
You've never killed someone in a game?

01:37.931 --> 01:41.059
We won't survive
without sacrificing others.

01:45.688 --> 01:46.689
Go.

01:48.900 --> 01:50.026
Don't.

01:50.110 --> 01:51.111
Arisu!

01:51.194 --> 01:52.612
- Asshole!
- Hold him down!

01:55.698 --> 01:56.825
If you don't do it,

01:58.576 --> 02:00.286
we'll shoot him.

02:04.666 --> 02:05.708
Don't go.

02:06.876 --> 02:08.128
Please, Ikeno.

02:08.962 --> 02:10.547
There's got to be another way.

02:19.639 --> 02:20.598
Open.

02:36.990 --> 02:38.158
I'm sorry.

04:07.163 --> 04:08.331
I'm sorry.

04:23.179 --> 04:25.014
Four rounds left.

04:25.598 --> 04:28.434
Please choose an opponent
by touching them.

04:46.619 --> 04:47.662
Took long enough!

04:51.708 --> 04:52.709
I know.

04:53.710 --> 04:54.711
Did you do it?

05:00.842 --> 05:01.843
Yes.

05:10.351 --> 05:12.312
Well done.

05:14.772 --> 05:16.441
Round of applause. Go on!

05:20.153 --> 05:22.071
Well done.

05:44.802 --> 05:45.636
Where's Nobu?

05:46.137 --> 05:48.306
He said he'd be right back.

06:11.245 --> 06:12.080
Nobu?

06:18.669 --> 06:20.088
- Hey!
- Look.

06:20.797 --> 06:22.090
Let me go!

06:28.179 --> 06:31.099
He turned that brat into a zombie.

06:31.641 --> 06:32.517
"That brat"?

06:34.769 --> 06:36.145
You mean Nobu?

06:36.229 --> 06:37.105
That's right.

06:37.188 --> 06:38.481
Nobu…

06:40.358 --> 06:41.692
Where'd he go?

06:42.527 --> 06:45.029
I saw him walking alone.

06:46.239 --> 06:47.657
That bastard.

06:49.492 --> 06:50.618
Bring him here!

06:50.701 --> 06:52.286
- Okay!
- Got it!

06:53.454 --> 06:56.290
People are starting to hide the fact
that they've turned.

06:56.833 --> 06:59.836
Like that bastard, Masato,
and that brat, Nobu.

07:00.378 --> 07:02.588
There could be more zombies among us.

07:05.258 --> 07:06.259
You're right.

07:07.260 --> 07:09.220
I don't trust some of you.

07:21.441 --> 07:22.567
No.

07:24.026 --> 07:24.986
Not me.

07:25.069 --> 07:27.196
He's a drug user

07:27.905 --> 07:29.740
suffering from withdrawal.

07:30.616 --> 07:33.661
The person who started this group,
Rei, is a zombie.

07:35.496 --> 07:38.541
Come to think of it,
I haven't seen her around.

07:39.667 --> 07:43.754
She might be a spy for the zombies.

07:45.131 --> 07:46.299
What?

07:46.382 --> 07:49.886
Does she really have a Vaccine card?

07:50.470 --> 07:52.096
What if it was all a lie?

07:53.347 --> 07:58.186
What if she came here
to make more zombies?

08:07.361 --> 08:09.739
The game's almost over.

08:13.409 --> 08:15.745
Let's get rid of our zombies too.

08:16.621 --> 08:18.998
We'll just shoot them all.

08:43.981 --> 08:46.317
No, don't.

08:52.240 --> 08:53.324
That hurts!

08:56.494 --> 08:57.495
Hey!

08:57.578 --> 08:58.788
Stop!

08:58.871 --> 09:00.206
He's making a run for it!

09:17.682 --> 09:18.516
Hey!

09:20.351 --> 09:23.187
I've been looking for you. I need a favor.

09:23.896 --> 09:24.772
What is it?

09:25.273 --> 09:27.817
Would you use your Vaccine card on me?

09:28.568 --> 09:29.443
There he is!

09:34.073 --> 09:35.032
Don't run!

09:35.116 --> 09:36.617
Stop it!

09:37.994 --> 09:40.246
- Stand up!
- Three rounds left.

09:40.955 --> 09:44.208
Please choose an opponent
by touching them.

09:47.211 --> 09:48.212
These guys…

09:49.088 --> 09:50.631
Shoot 'em all!

09:51.674 --> 09:52.508
Stand up.

10:04.770 --> 10:06.564
Please place your cards.

10:34.800 --> 10:35.635
Nobu.

10:37.845 --> 10:39.013
You're a zombie.

10:40.348 --> 10:41.182
What?

10:42.391 --> 10:43.559
I can tell.

10:45.811 --> 10:46.729
Listen.

10:47.229 --> 10:49.106
Do exactly as I say.

10:53.611 --> 11:00.368
Unfortunately, the zombies have spread
even more than you guys think.

11:01.035 --> 11:04.538
You might be better off as a zombie too.

11:07.375 --> 11:08.793
How would you know that?

11:10.086 --> 11:16.050
People have feelings,
which makes it difficult to kill others.

11:16.676 --> 11:21.263
And they'll hesitate to use
their precious Vaccine card on others.

11:22.014 --> 11:27.561
Zombies rapidly multiply
while they hold on to their cards.

11:28.813 --> 11:30.564
Once you've been turned,

11:30.648 --> 11:34.110
there's no reason
to not use your Zombie card.

11:35.695 --> 11:39.990
There were four zombies
when the game started.

11:40.074 --> 11:45.162
If the infection proceeded exponentially,
as one might expect,

11:45.246 --> 11:49.166
zombies would become
the majority in a mere

11:50.167 --> 11:51.544
three rounds.

11:54.630 --> 11:57.383
Don't you see which side
has the advantage?

12:00.386 --> 12:01.679
Did you really think

12:02.972 --> 12:04.348
I'd buy that?

12:04.432 --> 12:07.226
That's totally up to you.

12:07.727 --> 12:13.315
Either I get shot and die now
and you die at the end of the game,

12:14.108 --> 12:19.780
or you accept my deal now,
become a zombie, and survive.

12:43.053 --> 12:43.971
Open.

13:05.201 --> 13:08.996
I'm afraid I'm gonna pass on that deal.

13:31.936 --> 13:33.062
Masato.

13:34.271 --> 13:36.690
- We're too late.
- It's no use.

13:37.191 --> 13:38.192
Rei's in danger.

13:38.275 --> 13:40.444
- It's over!
- Nobu.

13:40.528 --> 13:41.821
- I'm dead!
- Nobu!

13:43.656 --> 13:44.949
Do what I said.

14:00.631 --> 14:02.383
Now we'll win.

14:03.717 --> 14:04.927
This is…

14:06.470 --> 14:07.721
It's going too far!

14:08.556 --> 14:12.184
The zombies want to kill us
because we killed their teammates.

14:13.310 --> 14:18.023
But zombies can't kill humans
in this game.

14:19.316 --> 14:22.820
Go ahead and become a zombie
if you wanna die too.

14:26.532 --> 14:29.618
Those guys are bad news.
They're going insane.

14:33.163 --> 14:34.540
Nobu!

14:35.165 --> 14:36.667
Over here. Hurry!

14:40.754 --> 14:41.589
What happened?

14:42.464 --> 14:43.465
Please listen.

14:55.769 --> 14:56.770
What's wrong?

15:04.904 --> 15:05.946
I was tricked.

15:32.389 --> 15:33.265
Rei.

15:41.774 --> 15:43.067
You're alive.

15:46.820 --> 15:48.614
Two rounds left.

15:49.281 --> 15:52.076
- Please choose an opponent by…
- Find them!

15:54.912 --> 15:56.830
Why play me?

15:58.958 --> 16:01.043
Which side do you think will win?

16:06.715 --> 16:07.967
The zombies.

16:10.427 --> 16:12.054
That was your conclusion all along.

16:12.554 --> 16:13.472
Well, yeah.

16:14.014 --> 16:17.726
Either the zombies win
through exponential growth,

16:17.810 --> 16:21.438
or humans freak out
and win by killing tons of zombies.

16:22.022 --> 16:24.316
It was going to be one or the other.

16:26.485 --> 16:27.319
Rei.

16:27.903 --> 16:28.821
What?

16:29.446 --> 16:30.739
You're not really

16:32.032 --> 16:33.117
a zombie, are you?

16:35.077 --> 16:37.121
Please place your cards.

16:42.668 --> 16:44.086
If you were a zombie,

16:45.170 --> 16:47.464
why build this barricade of trust?

16:48.507 --> 16:50.718
What was your endgame?

16:51.635 --> 16:56.849
You'd end up dead
if no one saved you with the vaccine.

16:59.059 --> 17:01.478
You thought gratitude would save you?

17:03.439 --> 17:07.276
A strategist like you
wouldn't risk her life

17:07.776 --> 17:10.112
on a plan that depends on gratitude.

17:11.321 --> 17:13.198
I see.

17:14.074 --> 17:18.579
But if you aren't really a zombie,

17:19.621 --> 17:21.498
then your plan is perfect.

17:22.875 --> 17:24.585
Is that really possible?

17:26.253 --> 17:29.006
Even if you didn't have a Zombie card,

17:29.965 --> 17:34.219
as long as everyone believed
your reasoning and it built trust,

17:35.220 --> 17:36.638
then, yes, it's possible.

17:38.599 --> 17:42.519
The barricade of trust was built on a lie.

17:43.645 --> 17:47.441
But trust is born when people believe you.

17:50.694 --> 17:53.155
I see what you mean.

17:53.238 --> 17:57.242
And that's also why you survived
your game against Ikeno.

17:59.328 --> 18:01.663
Ikeno used his Shotgun card, didn't he?

18:02.372 --> 18:04.124
But you didn't die.

18:04.750 --> 18:06.835
That's because you're not a zombie.

18:09.338 --> 18:10.339
Open.

18:20.265 --> 18:21.183
So?

18:22.184 --> 18:25.270
Why did you come to play me?

18:26.271 --> 18:28.398
To save you, Rei.

18:38.242 --> 18:39.159
You're a zombie?

18:45.332 --> 18:50.129
And here I thought
people like you don't lie.

18:56.301 --> 18:57.761
Now you're a zombie too.

18:58.762 --> 19:01.431
If you believed the zombies would win,

19:02.474 --> 19:04.351
why didn't you become one?

19:04.852 --> 19:08.981
I thought the zombies would win,
but I wasn't sure.

19:09.898 --> 19:13.902
When I built the barricade,
I thought the humans might win.

19:13.986 --> 19:15.737
That's why I built it.

19:18.699 --> 19:22.995
But I couldn't be sure,
so I waited to see how things played out.

19:23.912 --> 19:27.166
After watching Ikeno and his lackeys,

19:28.250 --> 19:30.836
I kinda started thinking

19:32.129 --> 19:33.964
human cruelty might win.

19:37.676 --> 19:39.011
But, Arisu,

19:39.720 --> 19:42.097
playing you convinced me.

19:43.182 --> 19:44.183
Thank you.

19:46.059 --> 19:48.604
The final round will now begin.

19:49.730 --> 19:50.856
We better hurry.

19:52.399 --> 19:54.484
How long were you a zombie?

19:56.361 --> 19:57.321
From the start.

20:01.700 --> 20:02.951
Sick move.

20:05.329 --> 20:06.371
Natsu!

20:08.540 --> 20:10.334
- Shion!
- Arisu!

20:15.088 --> 20:16.840
I got turned, like Nobu said.

20:16.924 --> 20:19.009
We can all turn in one more round.

20:20.844 --> 20:21.887
Where'd Nobu go?

20:22.554 --> 20:23.805
To find Tetsu.

20:35.025 --> 20:35.943
Shit.

20:36.443 --> 20:37.444
Tetsu!

20:38.904 --> 20:39.738
Tetsu?

20:46.078 --> 20:46.954
Please.

20:47.746 --> 20:48.997
Hear me out, please.

20:51.959 --> 20:52.793
Let me go!

20:57.089 --> 20:58.298
- Anyone there?
- Nope.

21:00.550 --> 21:02.636
Hey! Over here!

21:02.719 --> 21:04.263
Hey, let's go!

21:04.805 --> 21:05.722
After 'em!

21:19.403 --> 21:20.404
Stop!

21:26.034 --> 21:28.912
- Time's almost up! Find Tetsu!
- Got it!

21:34.459 --> 21:35.585
Tetsu!

21:43.510 --> 21:44.511
He's over here!

21:46.263 --> 21:47.264
This way!

21:47.347 --> 21:48.974
Found him over here!

21:54.730 --> 21:58.650
Please choose an opponent
by touching them.

21:58.734 --> 22:00.152
Nobu, the round's starting!

22:01.570 --> 22:04.072
Your Shotgun card's gone. Let's play!

22:08.285 --> 22:09.244
Open.

22:17.127 --> 22:18.003
Tetsu.

22:18.837 --> 22:19.713
Tetsu!

22:20.213 --> 22:21.506
I'll explain later.

22:30.098 --> 22:31.099
Shit!

22:33.143 --> 22:34.311
Kazuya.

22:36.229 --> 22:37.564
I just saved you.

22:39.941 --> 22:40.776
What?

22:42.736 --> 22:45.030
The final round is over.

22:48.158 --> 22:51.370
Here are the totals.

22:52.537 --> 22:53.497
Zombies,

22:54.373 --> 22:55.540
32.

22:56.875 --> 22:57.709
Humans,

22:59.503 --> 23:00.670
13.

23:01.880 --> 23:03.715
Zombies win.

23:05.967 --> 23:07.052
Yes!

23:07.677 --> 23:08.887
We did it!

23:10.722 --> 23:11.890
Thank goodness!

23:19.773 --> 23:24.945
There were fewer humans,
so it's game over for those 13 players.

23:32.411 --> 23:33.662
Seriously?

23:40.919 --> 23:42.587
All right!

23:46.091 --> 23:47.259
We won.

24:32.929 --> 24:34.055
Come with us.

25:05.921 --> 25:08.173
PLEASE PROCEED 16 KM SOUTHWEST

25:08.256 --> 25:11.426
THE "GAME" WILL BE HELD
AT SUNDOWN IN TWO DAYS

25:27.067 --> 25:28.693
Don't hold it against me.

25:35.450 --> 25:37.035
I wasn't going to.

25:38.870 --> 25:39.996
It's just a game.

25:41.831 --> 25:42.832
That it is.

25:48.588 --> 25:49.839
Let's get some sleep.

25:59.724 --> 26:03.520
Okay, your bedhead
won't be so bad tomorrow.

26:04.396 --> 26:06.398
Thanks, Big Sister.

26:06.481 --> 26:07.941
I'm not your sister.

26:16.241 --> 26:17.075
Huh?

26:18.577 --> 26:19.995
Isn't Arisu gonna sleep?

26:23.123 --> 26:25.208
I bet he's thinking about his wife.

26:28.753 --> 26:30.380
I'm jealous.

26:31.464 --> 26:37.053
My husband is
quick to yell at me and hit me.

26:38.471 --> 26:40.724
I've wished him dead so many times.

26:43.643 --> 26:46.646
It must be nice
to love someone with all your heart.

26:53.903 --> 26:54.738
Hey!

26:54.821 --> 26:56.239
- Stop it!
- Damn you!

28:01.346 --> 28:03.348
- Arisu…
- Wanna come over?

28:06.142 --> 28:07.268
What's wrong?

28:08.520 --> 28:09.521
Where are you?

28:14.734 --> 28:15.735
Arisu…

28:17.654 --> 28:18.613
Yeah?

28:20.031 --> 28:21.116
I'll come get you.

28:37.799 --> 28:38.675
Usagi?

28:39.968 --> 28:40.969
I'm sorry.

28:41.052 --> 28:42.053
Usa--

28:43.012 --> 28:45.306
I'm sorry, Dad.

28:47.350 --> 28:48.935
When I dream,

28:50.478 --> 28:54.357
I can feel my dad's presence.

28:57.527 --> 28:59.070
I want to see him again.

29:00.947 --> 29:02.365
If I can see my dad,

29:04.492 --> 29:06.453
I don't care if it's a nightmare.

29:12.125 --> 29:13.960
Please, Dad.

29:14.586 --> 29:16.129
Dad, please! Don't go!

29:17.046 --> 29:18.047
Don't go!

29:26.222 --> 29:28.683
I want to ask you about your father.

29:31.770 --> 29:33.146
Would you help me?

29:35.899 --> 29:37.484
If my dad is there…

29:39.819 --> 29:41.613
Even if it's a nightmare…

29:44.449 --> 29:45.742
I want to be there.

30:29.118 --> 30:30.578
For real?!

31:15.415 --> 31:16.291
Look out!

31:18.459 --> 31:19.586
People aren't shields!

31:20.503 --> 31:22.422
Just worry about yourself.

31:34.893 --> 31:35.810
Move!

32:04.255 --> 32:05.256
This way!

32:14.390 --> 32:16.017
Ryuji, follow my lead.

32:43.628 --> 32:46.047
Can't believe you survived like that.

32:46.965 --> 32:49.884
I managed somehow. And I had some help.

32:50.677 --> 32:52.679
Usagi, are you an athlete or what?

32:53.554 --> 32:54.555
Nope.

32:56.015 --> 32:57.600
I climb mountains for fun.

32:59.143 --> 33:01.813
I feel like I've met you before.

33:03.982 --> 33:07.735
So Usagi is your last name,
not a nickname?

33:08.319 --> 33:09.278
"Usagi."

33:09.779 --> 33:10.613
Yeah.

33:12.699 --> 33:14.450
Was your dad a mountain climber?

33:15.868 --> 33:18.913
I must've recognized you
from the gossip magazines.

33:18.997 --> 33:21.958
That mountain climber in the headlines?

33:22.041 --> 33:24.210
He killed himself
after lying about a climb.

33:24.293 --> 33:25.128
Yeah, him.

33:27.213 --> 33:28.047
Oh.

33:28.840 --> 33:29.841
Sorry.

33:31.259 --> 33:34.262
It's the magazines' fault.
Don't let it bother you.

33:35.763 --> 33:37.473
- Hey.
- Well, it's true.

33:38.266 --> 33:39.851
Did he really kill himself?

33:40.685 --> 33:42.270
- Ask her.
- I can't do that.

33:42.353 --> 33:43.187
Just ask.

33:43.271 --> 33:45.857
Do you care what people like that say?

33:47.650 --> 33:50.319
My dad wasn't one to lie.

33:52.822 --> 33:54.240
He'd never kill himself.

33:57.869 --> 34:01.914
You say that,
but you have your doubts, don't you?

34:03.916 --> 34:05.251
If it weren't for you,

34:06.669 --> 34:08.963
I'd never have come back here.

34:09.756 --> 34:10.757
I wonder.

34:11.549 --> 34:14.719
When I first saw you,
I sensed we were alike.

34:16.137 --> 34:19.057
We can't escape
the death haunting our lives.

34:21.893 --> 34:24.687
You wanted to be with your dead father.

34:25.897 --> 34:28.900
Isn't that what you always felt,
deep in your heart?

34:29.984 --> 34:33.196
That's why you accepted my offer.

34:34.655 --> 34:37.325
I never wanted to come back here.

34:40.286 --> 34:42.080
Never wanted to make Arisu sad.

34:42.163 --> 34:44.290
Deep inside, you felt differently.

34:44.373 --> 34:46.334
No, I'm not like you.

34:49.045 --> 34:52.131
I've always wanted to come here.

34:52.924 --> 34:58.888
I want to see the world of death
that lies beyond this borderland.

35:16.239 --> 35:18.366
I knew you'd be the one to survive.

35:20.660 --> 35:21.536
You…

35:23.955 --> 35:24.872
Who are you?

35:26.624 --> 35:27.834
You know who I am?

35:29.293 --> 35:30.128
Yes.

35:30.878 --> 35:34.257
I've devoted myself
to finding people like you.

35:35.383 --> 35:38.302
People qualified to become able citizens.

35:40.179 --> 35:41.013
Citizens?

35:43.641 --> 35:45.852
You've already been there, right?

35:46.727 --> 35:51.858
You made it to the end,
surviving many games despite your legs.

35:53.693 --> 35:55.319
You should remember by now.

36:01.701 --> 36:03.327
I have a favor to ask.

36:04.287 --> 36:07.665
Bring a certain woman
you know to that land.

36:08.416 --> 36:12.253
In exchange, I'll show you
the world you seek.

36:13.963 --> 36:16.674
You want to see the afterlife, right?

36:17.925 --> 36:20.553
Beyond the land between life and death

36:20.636 --> 36:22.555
lies the real world of death.

36:25.433 --> 36:26.350
What'll it be?

36:27.351 --> 36:28.769
Do you accept my deal?

36:30.771 --> 36:34.567
Will I really get what I want?

36:35.651 --> 36:37.653
- Yes.
- But how do I do it?

36:38.779 --> 36:43.284
She still carries the shadow
of her dead father deep in her heart.

36:45.494 --> 36:48.289
She will come if you invite her.

36:48.998 --> 36:50.416
"Invite her"?

36:51.292 --> 36:52.293
How?

36:57.006 --> 36:58.382
Have her drink this.

37:00.509 --> 37:03.137
Then you'll get what you want.

37:05.431 --> 37:07.683
So, what will it be?

37:20.446 --> 37:21.447
All right.

37:24.784 --> 37:25.785
I'll do it.

37:43.469 --> 37:47.932
That guy, Ryuji,
actually brought her here.

37:50.268 --> 37:53.729
And Arisu came, too, just as you planned.

37:56.399 --> 37:58.359
Arisu won't ever part with Usagi.

37:59.527 --> 38:03.197
Human emotions are invisible threads.

38:03.906 --> 38:06.409
Tug on them, and they always respond.

38:08.286 --> 38:09.829
What will you do next?

38:11.455 --> 38:13.666
I'll make good use of Ryuji.

38:13.749 --> 38:15.084
He's a valuable asset.

38:17.670 --> 38:19.547
He's quite eccentric too.

38:20.548 --> 38:22.508
He wants to see the afterlife.

38:23.009 --> 38:27.680
Above all, emotional threads
are growing between him and Usagi.

38:28.764 --> 38:31.559
I'll control him by tugging those threads.

38:33.728 --> 38:36.105
The game is finally getting interesting.

38:41.861 --> 38:43.070
You're scary.

39:07.261 --> 39:10.139
The required number of teams
has been reached.

39:12.141 --> 39:13.893
The game will now commence.

39:16.270 --> 39:19.940
THE TRAIN IS ARRIVING

40:17.873 --> 40:21.669
NOT IN SERVICE

40:27.466 --> 40:29.760
The game is Runaway Train.

40:43.649 --> 40:48.612
Here are the rules.
This train operates autonomously.

40:49.280 --> 40:53.242
Try to make it to the front car
from the starting car.

40:53.325 --> 40:55.202
Once the stop siren sounds,

40:57.079 --> 41:00.249
you must stop the train
in order to win the game.

41:02.418 --> 41:06.422
Thirty seconds after you move
to the car ahead and the door locks,

41:06.505 --> 41:10.926
either oxygen or poison gas
will be released.

41:11.677 --> 41:12.720
"Poison gas"?

41:13.220 --> 41:15.514
Excluding this starting car,

41:15.598 --> 41:19.768
poison gas will be released
in four of the eight cars.

41:21.103 --> 41:26.150
Please decide whether
to put on a gas mask before then.

41:27.318 --> 41:30.488
Each player gets five gas cartridges.

41:31.655 --> 41:35.576
Please attach them to the intake
on the right side of your mask.

41:36.869 --> 41:41.624
The cartridges contain
a neutralizing agent for the poison gas.

41:42.958 --> 41:47.129
You cannot use
another player's cartridges.

41:48.756 --> 41:52.092
And you cannot return to the car you left.

41:54.553 --> 41:57.723
Now strap your cartridges to your arm

41:57.806 --> 42:00.059
and take your gas mask.

42:13.781 --> 42:15.241
Game start.

42:15.824 --> 42:18.327
Please move to the next car.

42:47.231 --> 42:48.482
What's with the bird?

42:50.943 --> 42:53.779
If the canary dies from the gas,

42:55.155 --> 42:56.532
we'll know it's poison.

42:57.866 --> 42:58.867
I see.

43:01.245 --> 43:03.872
Please make your choice.

43:42.745 --> 43:43.579
What now?

43:48.459 --> 43:49.460
Sohta.

44:04.016 --> 44:05.517
This isn't a gas car.

44:06.894 --> 44:07.895
Oh no.

44:08.395 --> 44:10.105
We just wasted a cartridge?

44:11.148 --> 44:13.025
No, it's fine.

44:13.901 --> 44:17.488
There are four gas cars.
We still have four cartridges.

44:30.834 --> 44:33.128
Please move to the next car.

44:45.641 --> 44:47.976
Please make your choice.

45:32.646 --> 45:33.772
It was poison gas!

45:34.398 --> 45:36.275
We're safe!

45:45.033 --> 45:48.454
CAR 3

45:48.537 --> 45:51.248
Please make your choice.

45:53.459 --> 45:54.543
What should we do?

45:58.255 --> 45:59.381
I'm not using it.

46:00.007 --> 46:00.841
Why not?

46:01.800 --> 46:04.928
Everyone is scared,
so they mask up in the first half.

46:05.846 --> 46:10.768
The game creator will count on that
and release poison gas in the second half.

46:14.521 --> 46:17.691
- I'll try without it.
- That's just rolling the dice.

46:18.567 --> 46:20.194
There might be another way.

46:21.111 --> 46:24.156
We're in the third car. Five more to go.

46:24.239 --> 46:27.743
Three have poison gas,
and we have three cartridges left.

46:30.996 --> 46:32.498
What should we do?

46:36.293 --> 46:37.419
We won't wear them.

46:39.379 --> 46:41.298
What if your brother's wrong?

46:41.381 --> 46:43.801
- What's your problem?
- Chill out.

47:24.842 --> 47:26.969
Nothing you can do if it's poison.

47:39.898 --> 47:40.941
It's not poison.

47:41.024 --> 47:42.401
Thank goodness!

47:48.532 --> 47:49.825
What a relief.

47:49.908 --> 47:51.201
We're safe.

48:18.020 --> 48:19.396
It's bound for Asakusa!

48:20.397 --> 48:23.775
It runs parallel
to Omotesando and Aoyama-Itchome!

48:23.859 --> 48:24.735
A train nerd?

49:05.108 --> 49:07.903
We won't make it
if we wear our masks next time

49:08.570 --> 49:10.322
and it's not a gas car.

49:13.033 --> 49:15.953
You seem to know a lot about trains.

49:17.955 --> 49:18.789
Yeah.

49:19.289 --> 49:23.585
It looked like the people we just saw
took a while to die.

49:23.669 --> 49:26.171
So I bet it's a nerve gas
heavier than air.

49:26.672 --> 49:29.257
You'd need a lot to fill a car.

49:29.883 --> 49:32.886
- And?
- There have to be tanks for the gas.

49:33.387 --> 49:36.390
The poison gas cars
likely need space for them.

49:36.473 --> 49:37.474
Any ideas?

49:38.141 --> 49:40.143
There's no way I'd know that.

49:40.227 --> 49:43.063
We're running out of time.
We gotta decide!

49:44.898 --> 49:46.274
The train that went by…

49:46.942 --> 49:48.944
Maybe it was a trick.

49:49.027 --> 49:51.655
They could be trying to scare us.

49:51.738 --> 49:52.739
It's possible.

49:53.240 --> 49:56.576
We won't have enough cartridges
if we use our masks now.

49:58.620 --> 49:59.454
Wait.

50:03.583 --> 50:07.713
I'm not completely sure,
but this type of car

50:08.588 --> 50:10.716
shouldn't have a pantograph.

50:11.299 --> 50:12.592
A pantograph?

50:13.427 --> 50:14.553
On the roof?

50:14.636 --> 50:15.595
Yes.

50:16.096 --> 50:18.390
It allows the train to draw power.

50:18.890 --> 50:23.437
If there's a pantograph,
it will occupy a lot of roof space.

50:24.104 --> 50:28.066
But this car shouldn't have one.

50:29.526 --> 50:33.655
So you're saying
there's space for a gas tank?

50:36.867 --> 50:38.785
Yes, most likely.

50:40.537 --> 50:41.538
"Most likely"?

50:42.289 --> 50:43.832
I'm gonna trust that?

50:46.168 --> 50:48.462
Please make your choice.

50:53.425 --> 50:54.342
What do we do?

50:54.426 --> 50:55.427
What now?

52:17.634 --> 52:19.594
- I'm sorry!
- Yuna!

53:04.556 --> 53:06.850
CAR 5

53:14.274 --> 53:16.359
Four cars left, including this one.

53:16.860 --> 53:22.073
There are still two poison gas cars,
and we only have two cartridges left.

53:23.033 --> 53:24.034
How about this car?

53:26.411 --> 53:27.579
This car

53:28.580 --> 53:30.624
should have a pantograph.

53:31.291 --> 53:34.502
So there's no space for a gas tank.

54:22.884 --> 54:25.971
CAR 6

54:28.098 --> 54:29.099
Wait.

54:32.102 --> 54:33.645
These racks are wrong.

54:35.397 --> 54:37.274
- I see.
- What is it?

54:39.901 --> 54:42.904
I'm sorry. I got the model wrong.

54:43.613 --> 54:47.158
- What?
- It's a different train model.

54:47.659 --> 54:51.121
So the pantograph locations differ too.

54:52.872 --> 54:55.709
I'm sorry! I don't know what to do now.

54:58.420 --> 55:00.171
So we just got lucky?

55:01.881 --> 55:02.841
That's right.

55:02.924 --> 55:04.217
You asshole!

55:04.801 --> 55:06.303
Aren't you a train nerd?!

55:06.386 --> 55:08.179
- Well?!
- Stop it!

55:09.431 --> 55:10.473
There's no time.

55:12.392 --> 55:14.894
Please make your choice.

55:16.313 --> 55:17.605
Two cartridges left.

55:17.689 --> 55:18.565
CAR 6

55:18.648 --> 55:20.275
And two more gas cars.

55:20.817 --> 55:22.861
We can't make a single mistake.

55:36.875 --> 55:38.251
So it's up to a hunch?

55:40.503 --> 55:41.338
Yep.

55:48.470 --> 55:51.681
I'll bet… on her hunch.

55:56.519 --> 55:57.604
Me too.

55:59.064 --> 56:00.315
My bet is on Usagi.

56:01.399 --> 56:02.734
This might just work.

56:08.365 --> 56:09.699
Sounds good to me.

56:13.995 --> 56:15.622
A test of luck at the end.

56:32.680 --> 56:37.143
Come on, poison gas.

56:59.707 --> 57:00.708
It's alive.

57:01.668 --> 57:03.086
This isn't a gas car!

59:36.864 --> 59:39.534
Subtitle translation by: Jason Franzman
